SparkScout — third-party data and attribution notice
=====================================================

SparkScout accesses public energy data published by the International
Renewable Energy Agency (IRENA). The data and statistical indicators
delivered by this server are governed by IRENA's own terms of use:

  - Renewable capacity and generation statistics, public finance data,
    and cost series retrieved via the dataset tools
    (sparkscout_list_datasets, sparkscout_query_dataset,
     sparkscout_query_dataset_aggregations, sparkscout_get_dataset_value,
     sparkscout_sample_dataset) are subject to IRENA's licensing and
    attribution requirements. Every response carries a citation block
    with the precise dataset identifier and filter context; downstream
    users must retain that citation.

  - IRENA publication text (reports, working papers, briefs) returned
    by the report tools (sparkscout_list_reports, sparkscout_get_report,
     sparkscout_search_reports, sparkscout_answer_question) is covered
    by the publication's own copyright. Citation strings are produced
    via sparkscout_cite using each report's frontmatter citation block.

SparkScout itself is released under the LICENSE file in this repository.
The two are separate: this NOTICE governs how retrieved content may be
used, while LICENSE governs how the SparkScout source code may be used.
